GPU memory manager: addresses past the address space are unmapped

MemoryManager::GetEntry indexed its entry tables with any address. A garbage GPU address from a
command stream ran past the table and faulted, on the GPU threads:
- OOT on the console, nx2:vi2 guest wait: IsFullyMappedRange on 0x0308e4210a33cb00, GPUBack;
- on the PC: a garbage acquire address, 0x54f00000000 + 0x1000.
Every page lookup and range operation (MemoryOperation, so reads, writes, IsFullyMappedRange,
MaxContinuousRange) asks GetEntry first. An address at or past the address space size now reads
as Free, so callers take their unmapped path, as GpuToCpuAddress already did. One compare per
lookup.

--- a/src/video_core/memory_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/memory_manager.cpp
@@ -71,6 +71,12 @@
 MemoryManager::~MemoryManager() = default;
 
 MemoryManager::EntryType MemoryManager::GetEntry(size_t position, bool is_big_page) const {
+    // An address past the address space is unmapped. Every range operation (MemoryOperation, so
+    // IsFullyMappedRange, reads, writes) asks here first: a garbage GPU address from a command
+    // stream (0x0308e4210a33cb00 in an OOT run) indexed past the entry table and faulted.
+    if (position >= address_space_size) [[unlikely]] {
+        return EntryType::Free;
+    }
     if (is_big_page) {
         position = position >> big_page_bits;
         const u64 entry_mask = big_entries[position / 32];
